  "selected_complete_reports": 6,
  "scope": "Actual modeled bounded UInt64 shift/mask/Boolean bit equals its natural binary digit. Symbolic high-to-low bit recurrence reconstructs low count bits for arbitrary natural word/count/seed; actual64-bit member bounds and UInt64 width are internally derived, giving seed*2^64+word.toNat. Reversed arbitrary UInt64 word walk reconstructs seed*radix64^length+exact little-endian packWords, matching both pinned Rust pow loop schedules/bit selectors. The generic fold-agreement helper has a legitimate per-member transition equality interface; final loop/exponent conclusions discharge it internally and assume no desired exponent/meaning. Two original failed attempts retained (Lean lambda rewrite and physical pressure); only dsimp of the fold-step lambda added, second source byte-identical, contracts/algorithms/machine guards unchanged. Producer rejected-attempt summary1 is narrower than the two raw failed results and is retained unchanged. Six full standard-axiom theorem reports, no unrolled256-bit execution. Mathematical field-power fold, actual native UInt64/Choice/compiler/caller/private-constructor correspondence and full Transfer remain owned OPEN; no Root verifier/native/combined replay.",
